# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 and 8: `@Door`'s block ends on `@ door`, the plain part of its door's bundle, so `door <- @Door $called` binds the door's first value, asked at the build with the name its parameter holds there; the inlined widget's places take the page's next positions; the build reads the value (a plain `let`, a plain argument, a hold's initial value), and a click on "more" re-reads it in the label and in the hold's step.
test a_plain_result_is_bound_at_the_caller

tick 0
  added:
    0: Pad.Door(name="front")
    1: Ui.Label(text="inside door 1")
    2: Ui.Label(text="hello door 1")
    3: Ui.Label(text="sign door 1")
    4: Ui.Button(label="more")
    5: Ui.Label(text="door 1 knocked 0")
    6: Ui.Button(label="never")
  result: "door 1"

tick 1
  in:
    4: click
  changed:
    5: Ui.Label(text="door 1 knocked 1")
  result: "door 1, door 1"
